<p class="copy">
	The Protocols of Planar Exploration and Exploitation are the body of international law that governs how humanity opens, explores, and profits from other planes. Ratified by the UN in 2161, they set the terms for first contact with a plane’s native species and bar planar holding companies from directly manipulating or influencing the politics of parasapient cultures. <?php echo sf_lore_link('american-empire', 'The American Empire'); ?> refused to be a signatory.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	After <?php echo sf_lore_link('first-switch-gate-catastrophe', 'the first switch-gate catastrophe'); ?> erased New York City in 2175, the Protocols were expanded, and <?php echo sf_lore_link('bureau-of-planar-management', 'the Bureau of Planar Management and Enforcement'); ?> was founded to enforce them. The expansion of 2176 also broke <?php echo sf_lore_link('holy-oak-discovery-services', 'Holy Oak Discovery Services’'); ?> monopoly over humanity’s access to Co-H2O/E2, turning <?php echo sf_lore_link('leviathan', 'Leviathan'); ?> into a public plane. Even with its capital still smoldering, the Empire refused to ratify the expanded Protocols, and American holdings in deep space or American sovereign territory aren’t subject to Bureau scrutiny.
</p>
<p class="copy mb-0">
	In practice, compliance falls to the <?php echo sf_lore_link('explorers-lodge', 'Explorers’ Lodge'); ?>, whose representatives are licensed to provide inspection and certification services when a new gate is opened. On <?php echo sf_lore_link('tetra', 'Tetra'); ?>, home to both the UN and the SDU, planar industries operate in strict accordance with the Protocols.
</p>
